    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41825" root="ورب" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرِبٌ</span></b>  <i>Corrupt.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِرْقٌ وَرِب</span> <i>A corrupt
root, origin,</i> or <i>stock.</i> (S, K.) Aboo-Dharrah
El-Hudhalee says,
“<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنْ تَنْتَسِتْ تُنْسَبْ إِلَى عِرْقٍ وَرِبْ</span><br />
”
[<i>If thou mention thy lineage, thy lineage is
traced up to a corrupt origin,</i> or <i>stock</i>]. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ وَرِبٌ</span> <i>A corrupt man.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَرِبٌ</span> A
cloud <i>that is loose</i> (K) <i>and much broken.</i> (TA.)

